'' A USTRING CHAIN COMPARES AS A USTRING. Check types every '&' STRING, so 'u & "y" = "Uy"'
'' built the chain with fb_UStrConcat and then compared its UTF-16 bytes with the NARROW
'' fb_StrCompare against a narrow literal: every '=' and '<>' answered wrong, and an
'' ordering was right only by accident. Measured, fbc emits fb_UStrCompare against a UTF-16
'' literal, and prints eq where tiko printed ne.
''
'' SELECT CASE over one had the same flavour wrong, and once that was right, a SECOND
'' case value missed: the subject was not copied, and the first fb_UStrCompare released
'' the temporary. fbc copies it with fb_UStrInit, and 'case "Ux", "Uy"' prints hit.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/ustr-chain-compare.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_UStrConcat(
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_UStrCompare(
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_StrToUStr(
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_UStrInit(@$tmp
'' EXPECT-NOT: fb_StrCompare(
